drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'link the new report `duplicates` the existing ticket (...) or resume the existing one instead of filing.'","No stated condition distinguishing when to file-and-link versus resume-instead-of-filing (e.g. whether the existing ticket is open/in_progress vs. closed, or whether the symptom is identical vs. a regression).","T8(b): a decision rule is referenced but not fully specified for the LLM executor consuming this skill."],"finding":"Action (a) tracker sweep offers two mutually-exclusive outcome branches — link the new report `duplicates` the existing ticket, or resume the existing one instead of filing — but never states the decision rule that selects between them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2156653cb39820d","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (a) Tracker sweep; AC line for 'rebar search'","norm_id":"ne23f7c10db42e87d","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An existing CLOSED ticket matches the symptom (a regression): should the agent resume the closed ticket or file a new report linked `duplicates`?","An existing OPEN ticket matches: resume vs. link is left to the agent's discretion."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line rule to action (a): resume an existing OPEN/in_progress ticket in place; for a CLOSED match that is a regression, file the new report and link it `duplicates` the closed ticket; for a CLOSED match that is genuinely the same live behavior, reopen/resume rather than re-file.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":